                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Overcoming Pain is a game I received a code for on Keymailer, except the Keymailer listing called the game “Mysterious Oasis” for some reason.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=arXPSnEGVno\n\nI’m not sure how the developer managed to list another name for their game specifically on Keymailer, but that alone should show what you are in for if you are unfortunate enough to play this asset flip.\n\nAll of the content is purchased from the Unity store, which is something I am very used to dealing with these days. Both maps, the weapons, enemies, et cetera are just thrown into a shoddy product with little gameplay value.\n\nYou have two different maps to choose from, each with a day and night version. Both maps are incredibly small and not laid out in a way that makes a horde mode FPS enjoyable in the slightest. The weapons are placed in corners and dead ends which makes it nearly impossible to get one without being surrounded, there were no ammo pickups for weapons beyond the one or two you find next to the weapon on the ground. After you run out of ammo you just resort to melee until you die or the game ends.\n\nThere are three enemies in the game, all of which look like they are from completely different games. There are stock zombies, robots and soldiers. You can fight them alone or combine them together to make it look more like a child playing with toys from three different sets.\n\nThe soldiers and robots will shoot you with pinpoint accuracy, which is made even worse in the factory level which has nearly no cover. You will die in a few hits.\n\nThere is a slow motion effect that seems to randomly trigger when killing an enemy with no explanation. Everything is slowed, including your character and this makes it infuriating to deal with. For some reason even though the enemies move slower during this mode, they shoot you at the same speed which results in cheap deaths.\n\nYou can have an A.I teammate back you up, but he isn’t much help as he will deal friendly damage to you if you are in front of him when an enemy becomes visible. His model also only blinks with one eye for some reason and I find that hilarious.\n\nOvercoming Pain is a giant waste of time for anyone who plays it. Just get Left 4 Dead or any other real game if you want to shoot hordes of enemies.\n\nIf you found this review helpful, follow my curator page to see everything I cover. http://store.steampowered.com/curator/29029552/",
